1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,060
In October 2017, a North Carolina businessman named Michael Smith sent himself an email.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,460
According to a federal indictment, it was a business plan, written as a Rhythmatic.

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:17,540
52 cloud accounts, 20 bots on each, 1,040 fake listeners.

4
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:25,480
At half a cent a stream, the email projected $1,207,128 a year.

5
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:29,280
That email comes from the indictment. It's an allegation.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,820
This isn't. In March, 2026, Smith pleaded guilty to one count of conspiracy to commit wire fraud,

7
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:43,980
and agreed to a money judgment of $8,091,843.64.

8
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:47,720
He did the math. This is what it cost.

9
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:54,780
This isn't really a story about bots. It's about a pool of money that every artist on a streaming service shares,

10
00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:01,240
and about a new kind of song that prosecutors say let one man draw from that pool for years.

11
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:05,980
According to the indictment, the songs he needed weren't written by a person.

12
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:11,760
They came from an AI music company under a contract for up to 10,000 songs a month,

13
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:15,920
and at the center of this case sits a question nobody has answered.

14
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:22,440
Spotify says its protections held what Smith got from Spotify to a small fraction of the total.

15
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,540
So who paid the rest? The public record doesn't say.

16
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:32,680
On Tuesday, October 6th, a federal judge is set to decide what the rest of this costs him.

17
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:38,940
His lawyers argue, according to billboard, that each fake stream's effect was a drop in an ocean.

18
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:42,800
The prosecutor who announced his guilty plea put it differently.

19
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:46,200
The millions of dollars Smith stole was real.

20
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:51,060
Before any of this, there was a real music career, a small one.

21
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:56,880
Rolling Stone reported that Smith owned a chain of medical clinics, co-founded a record label,

22
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:03,300
and bankrolled a hip-hop competition on BET called One Shot, where he also sat as a judge.

23
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:08,840
He called it the first nationally televised competition specific to hip-hop.

24
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,500
That's the beauty of monitored. They can't manipulate it.

25
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:18,800
That's what a Nashville radio promoter told Rolling Stone about a 2017 single by Michael Smith,

26
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,840
Your My Kind of Beautiful.

27
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:25,560
Monitored charts are built on real stations reporting real spins.

28
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:30,340
The song peaked at number 35 on billboards adult contemporary chart.

29
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:36,740
The next year, an album Smith made with a collaborator reached number one on billboards jazz charts.

30
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:37,900
He posted,

31
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,760
I officially have a number one billboard album.

32
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:46,200
The federal case against him isn't about those charts. It's about streaming royalties.

33
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:54,560
In October 2017, according to a federal indictment, Smith emailed himself a plan for one thousand forty bought accounts.

34
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:59,240
He later pleaded guilty to one count of conspiracy to commit wire fraud.

35
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:03,200
To see why that plan could pay, you need one idea.

36
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,740
Streaming services don't pay a fixed price per play.

37
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,560
They put a share of their revenue into a pool.

38
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:13,480
Then the pool is split by each rights holder share of all the streams.

39
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:15,880
Picture a simplified pot.

40
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,520
One hundred dollars and one hundred streams.

41
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:23,080
Each stream is worth a dollar. Add one hundred fake streams.

42
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:27,260
The pot doesn't grow. Every stream is now worth fifty cents.

43
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:32,740
The artist behind the one hundred real streams now split fifty dollars instead of one hundred.

44
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:36,100
That's our illustration, not a number from the case.

45
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,000
So a fake stream doesn't create new money.

46
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
In the prosecutors telling, it takes a slice of the same pot.

47
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:47,000
Money that would otherwise go to artists that real people chose to hear.

48
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:48,720
Hold onto that pot.

49
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:54,160
By the end, the hardest question in this case is who actually lost money from it?

50
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:59,180
By May 2017, according to the indictment, Smith was emailing an associate.

51
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,500
Make up names and addresses.

52
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:05,680
He bought fake email accounts in bulk, the indictment says,

53
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,860
and registered bought accounts under made up names.

54
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:12,740
Often on family plans, because they cost less per user.

55
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:18,579
The bots, prosecutors say, ran in browser tabs on rented cloud computers,

56
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:24,800
with modified macros looping the music, and VPNs hiding that it all ran from his home.

57
00:04:25,459 --> 00:04:30,040
The indictment says he told his helpers the setup had to be undetectable.

58
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:32,560
But the machine had a weak point.

59
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:35,440
It wasn't the bots, it was the songs.

60
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:39,600
Put a billion streams on one track, and someone notices.

61
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:45,600
Spread them across tens of thousands of tracks, and each one is played only a few times.

62
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:49,780
That, prosecutors say, is why he needed more music.

63
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:54,680
In May 2019, according to the indictment, he put it plainly.

64
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:58,560
If we get too many streams on one song, it comes down.

65
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:00,980
Then the warning started.

66
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:05,220
I acknowledge what you wrote, and I ask that you still release it.

67
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:09,400
Prosecutors say Michael Smith wrote that in March 2018.

68
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:13,860
After a music distribution company warned him that one of his songs

69
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:18,300
fit the criteria that is usually linked to store-end streaming abuse.

70
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:19,600
He added,

71
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:22,860
we have no intentions of committing streaming fraud.

72
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:29,580
That October, after what the company called multiple reports of streaming abuse from different stores,

73
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,640
he replied,

74
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,760
this is absolutely wrong and crazy.

75
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:37,100
There is absolutely no fraud going on whatsoever.

76
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:38,920
How can I appeal this?

77
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
In March 2019, he told the streaming platform,

78
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,760
you have slandered me to my distributors.

79
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:51,780
Every one of those lines is written into the federal charge Smith later pleaded guilty to,

80
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,420
conspiracy to commit wire fraud.

81
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:58,580
That charge calls his 2019 statements false.

82
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:04,420
Smith own catalog, the indictment says, was not nearly large enough.

83
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,800
He tried a publicist catalog.

84
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,840
He even tried selling fake streams as a service.

85
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:16,920
On October 4, 2018, according to the indictment, he wrote to two associates.

86
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,900
In order to not raise any issues with the powers that be,

87
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:24,340
we need a ton of content with small amounts of streams.

88
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:27,320
The answer was already arriving.

89
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:34,340
According to the indictment, that year, Smith began working with the chief executive of an AI music company,

90
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:36,280
and with a music promoter.

91
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:43,100
By October 18, Smith was reporting hundreds of thousands of streams on AI-made tracks.

92
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:47,820
The promoter, who had called it a proof of concept, wrote back,

93
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:50,380
we've proved the model works.

94
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,480
Up to 10,000 songs a month.

95
00:06:54,240 --> 00:07:00,000
According to a federal indictment, that's what Michael Smith contracted for in February 2019,

96
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:03,540
with the chief executive of an AI music company.

97
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:06,920
It was called a master services agreement.

98
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:14,200
Under it, the indictment says, Smith would own the song's outright and supply the song and artist names.

99
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:22,060
The AI company would get $2,000 a month, or 15% of the streaming revenue, whichever was greater.

100
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,720
The files arrived named like random code.

101
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:30,680
Smith, prosecutors say, gave them fake song and artist names.

102
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:37,380
Songs called Zygophicia, Zygotic Wash Stands, Zyme Bedouin.

103
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:45,540
Artists called Kaliope Bloom, Calm Knuckles, Calorie Screams, and Camel Edible.

104
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:50,520
A month later, the indictment says, the AI executive wrote to him.

105
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:54,060
This is not music, it's instant music.

106
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:59,840
The executive isn't named in court papers, and neither is the promoter who worked with them.

107
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:02,440
Neither has been publicly charged.

108
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:06,760
Smith has pleaded guilty to conspiracy to commit wire fraud.

109
00:08:07,419 --> 00:08:12,140
On June 5, 2019, according to the indictment, Smith wrote,

110
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:15,920
we're at 88 million total streams so far.

111
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:22,160
He told his two partners the streams were earning about $110,000 a month,

112
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:30,040
that each of them was getting 10%, and he asked for another 10,000 songs to spread this out more.

113
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:33,179
The next year's ran on the same engine, only bigger.

114
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:37,520
August 2020, the AI executive per the indictment.

115
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:43,179
Song quality is 10x to 20x better now, and we also have vocal generation capabilities.

116
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:49,520
At certain points, prosecutors alleged, Smith had as many as 10,000 active body counts.

117
00:08:50,159 --> 00:08:51,740
Those accounts had to be paid for.

118
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:59,940
From about 2020 to 2023, the indictment alleges, Smith moved $1.3 million of royalties

119
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:04,920
through an account called SMH Entertainment into a Manhattan debit card service,

120
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:09,000
using dozens of fake employee names to pay for body counts.

121
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,380
That became a money laundering charge.

122
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,420
It is not part of the charge he pleaded guilty to.

123
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:16,560
Mike is the human author.

124
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:20,760
That's what Michael Smith's representatives wrote in March 2023,

125
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:25,120
according to a federal indictment, after the songwriter's royalty collective,

126
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,700
the MLC, stopped paying him.

127
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,840
In the same exchange, they wrote,

128
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:33,380
Mike categorically denies any play manipulation.

129
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:39,940
According to the same indictment, an AI company had been supplying him songs under contract since 2019.

130
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:45,240
When Smith was arrested the next year, the MLC's chief executive said it had

131
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:48,480
withheld payment of the associated mechanical royalties.

132
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,500
The MLC hasn't said how much it held back.

133
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:55,220
Smith later pleaded guilty to conspiracy to commit wire fraud.

134
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,380
The rest is the indictment's account.

135
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:02,980
In February 2024, less than a year after the MLC stopped paying him,

136
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:08,060
Smith wrote, per the indictment, that his music had generated at this point

137
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:13,160
over four billion streams and $12 million in royalties since 2019.

138
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,640
That's his own number, as prosecutors quoted, not a finding.

139
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:21,000
Remember it, the numbers in this case keep changing.

140
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,860
On the morning of Wednesday, September 4, 2024,

141
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,860
Smith was arrested at his home outside Charlotte.

142
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:32,960
The same day, the Justice Department announced what it called the first criminal case

143
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,600
involving artificially inflated music streaming.

144
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:41,480
Three counts, wire fraud conspiracy, wire fraud, and money laundering conspiracy.

145
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,000
Each carried up to 20 years in prison.

146
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:48,640
Prosecutors alleged he had obtained more than $10 million in royalties.

147
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,860
The US Attorney at the time said,

148
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,360
it's time for Smith to face the music.

149
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,540
Smith's lawyer declined to comment.

150
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:59,800
He was released on a $500,000 personal reconnaissance bond.

151
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,900
The case headed toward trial.

152
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:07,900
In early 2026, Rolling Stone reported it was expected to start on October 6th.

153
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,080
There was no trial.

154
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:12,620
Three federal counts, up to 20 years each.

155
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:18,280
Michael Smith, indicted in 2024, never pleaded guilty to any of them.

156
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:25,760
Instead, on March 19th, 2026, prosecutors filed a brand new one-count charge.

157
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:31,960
Conspiracy to commit wire fraud under a different statute, section 371.

158
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:37,320
Smith gave up his right to an indictment and was charged on it that same day.

159
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:42,600
Same kind of crime, a different law, with a much lower ceiling.

160
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:48,700
He pleaded guilty to it before US District Judge John Kotl under a plea agreement.

161
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:51,460
The agreement itself isn't public.

162
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,740
The maximum he faces on it?

163
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,080
Five years, not 20.

164
00:11:57,140 --> 00:12:00,520
It is a federal conviction, and it came with a price.

165
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:07,260
A money judgment of $8 million, $91,843.64.

166
00:12:08,079 --> 00:12:12,400
As of late September, 2026, he had not been sentenced.

167
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:18,260
There's a sentence in the Forfeiture Order, Michael Smith agreed to after his guilty plea

168
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:22,080
that sounds like a confession that millions of dollars vanished.

169
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:23,620
It isn't.

170
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:30,940
The order sets his money judgment, $8 million in change, as the proceeds he personally obtained.

171
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:37,840
And in it, he admits those proceeds cannot be located upon the exercise of due diligence.

172
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:39,960
It sounds dramatic.

173
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:45,580
It's actually a legal formula, the trigger words from the federal Forfeiture Statute.

174
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:49,920
The same words were already in his 2024 indictment.

175
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:52,220
What they do is practical.

176
00:12:52,900 --> 00:12:58,460
They let the government go after his other property instead, up to whatever remains unpaid.

177
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:03,520
So the $8 million is a debt the court has entered against him.

178
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:07,900
Final as to him, and set to become part of his sentence.

179
00:13:09,140 --> 00:13:12,920
No public document we found says whether any of it has been collected.

180
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,520
Now line the numbers up.

181
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:20,040
His own email, as the indictment quotes it, claimed $12 million.

182
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:23,520
The indictment alleged more than $10 million.

183
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,200
The judgment?

184
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,040
Just over $8 million.

185
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,900
Why the figure fell from $10 to $8?

186
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:33,600
The public record we reviewed doesn't explain.

187
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:37,540
Which leaves the question this whole case keeps circling.

188
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:42,380
$8 million in royalties by the Justice Department's count.

189
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,380
Whose money was it?

190
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:50,260
Spotify says Michael Smith got only about $60,000 from Spotify.

191
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:57,920
He has pleaded guilty to conspiracy to commit wire fraud and agreed to a money judgment of more than $8 million.

192
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:00,600
So who paid him?

193
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,640
Spotify's answer came eight days after his arrest.

194
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:16,580
Its measures it said limited the royalties Smith was able to game from Spotify to approximately $60,000 of the $10 million noted in the indictment.

195
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:22,040
Spotify says it usually accounts for about half of all streams in the market.

196
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:27,040
Pandora put its estimated royalty exposure at $1,500.

197
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:34,240
The songwriter's collective, the MLC, says it caught him early and withheld payment.

198
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:44,560
When digital music news asked Apple music, boom play, title, YouTube and Amazon music what they paid him, none of them responded.

199
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:47,320
Soundcloud wouldn't give a figure.

200
00:14:48,300 --> 00:14:51,120
Not answering isn't an answer, either way.

201
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:54,100
These are the company's own accounts.

202
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:59,000
Which services paid most of the money has never been publicly established.

203
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:12,220
Michael Lewin, who runs an industry anti-fraud group, the Music Fights Fraud Alliance, was speaking about streaming fraud industry-wide, not about Smith's case when he told Rolling Stone.

204
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:21,920
If you view it as one or five or ten percent, that is a percentage of royalties not going to artists, creators and songwriters.

205
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:29,840
He also said he hadn't seen a trusted percentage or number for how big streaming fraud really is.

206
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:36,320
The head of the recording industry's global body, IFPI, puts it more bluntly.

207
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:39,400
This is theft, plain and simple.

208
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:44,760
Money that, prosecutors say, came out of real artist's share.

209
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:49,380
Spreads so thin, it's hard to point to any one artist's slice.

210
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:53,960
That gap is where Smith's lawyers built their case for mercy.

211
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:59,320
On September 22nd, 2026, Smith's lawyers filed their sentencing memo.

212
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:04,820
Michael Smith's lawyers have a metaphor for the fraud conspiracy he pleaded guilty to.

213
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:08,740
According to Billboard, we haven't seen the memo ourselves.

214
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:10,820
Their sentencing memo says,

215
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:19,660
The effect each individual stream of one artist's song has on every other artist's share of total streams is not akin to a drop in a proverbial bucket.

216
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:21,560
It is a drop in an ocean.

217
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:28,480
And, no individual artist or songwriter suffered any perceptible harm from Mr. Smith's conduct.

218
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:30,500
They're asking for probation.

219
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:38,720
Billboard reports the sentencing guidelines call for 46 to 57 months and the probation office recommended 24.

220
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:41,080
The maximum is 5 years.

221
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:49,480
In May, his lawyers questioned whether the section 2B1.1 guidelines fairly address Mr. Smith's culpability.

222
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:53,080
That's the fraud guideline and it scales with loss.

223
00:16:53,940 --> 00:16:57,060
If the loss is spread across an ocean, how do you measure it?

224
00:16:57,060 --> 00:17:00,600
Sentencing was set for October 6th, 2026.

225
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,760
That's when Judge Koldle decides how much a drop in an ocean costs.

226
00:17:05,619 --> 00:17:06,839
The memo goes further.

227
00:17:07,339 --> 00:17:14,680
Per Billboard, it argues that bot-driven fraud is indisputably rampant, including by big labels and publishers.

228
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:17,119
That is the defense's claim.

229
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:20,960
It points to no criminal record and to letters of support.

230
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:25,980
While he made serious mistakes here, those mistakes do not define him as a person.

231
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:31,720
A rapper who worked with Smith on one shot, KXNG Crooked, told Rolling Stone.

232
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,720
Whatever he did, he made that bed and he's got a lie in it.

233
00:17:36,339 --> 00:17:40,720
But he added, let's not take the man who's the independent guy and string him up.

234
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:46,619
In 2018, according to the indictment, Smith's problem was that he couldn't get enough songs.

235
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:55,960
At its June 2026 peak, one streaming service, Deezer, says it was receiving nearly 90,000 fully AI-generated trucks.

236
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:58,980
More than half of everything uploaded.

237
00:17:59,820 --> 00:18:04,680
Deezer says AI music makes up only 1-3% of streams on Deezer.

238
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:10,820
But that up to 85% of those streams in 2025 were fraudulent and were demonetized.

239
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:18,940
And it says the impact on human-artist royalties is minimal on Deezer because it strips those streams out of the pool.

240
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:28,320
On September 14, 2026, the Recording Industry Body IFPI launched a Streaming Integrity Initiative,

241
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:33,880
asking distributors to verify their customers and vet uploads for AI-related risks.

242
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,360
Universal, Sony and Warner signed on.

243
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:39,860
The industry has also gone to court.

244
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:44,500
Against distributors, the companies that deliver music to the streaming services.

245
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:59,900
In 2024, UMG and other music companies sued one of them, believe, and its tune-core service, seeking at least $500 million over uploads under names like Kendrick Lamar and Juten Bieber.

246
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:03,600
Believe said it strongly refuted the claims.

247
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:08,300
In April 2026, the case was dismissed after a settlement.

248
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:13,240
Terms weren't disclosed. No admission of wrongdoing has been made public.

249
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:19,020
The newest fight is a separate one, a civil lawsuit about uploads and copyright.

250
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:21,980
It is not part of Smith's criminal case.

251
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:27,440
4,562 tracks in 12 months from one account.

252
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:33,220
That's what Universal Music Group alleges about the busiest account on the distributor distro kid.

253
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:38,820
In a lawsuit filed September 15, 2026, in federal court in Delaware.

254
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:43,840
The suit claims deceptive trade practices and copyright infringement.

255
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:54,860
At two other high-volume accounts, the complaint alleges, over 97 and over 98% of the tracks are raw outputs from the AI Generator Soono.

256
00:19:55,680 --> 00:20:04,680
And it alleges distro kid accounts for more than half of weekly track releases on one major service, nearly 12 million tracks in six months.

257
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:07,460
UMG also draws a line.

258
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:14,280
This lawsuit is not about the distribution of AI-generated music when clearly disclosed as such.

259
00:20:15,180 --> 00:20:16,280
Distro kid's response.

260
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:19,800
We strongly disagree with UMG's allegations.

261
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:25,160
We are confident in our practices and intend to defend distro kid vigorously.

262
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:31,780
These are allegations in a civil case that has only just been filed. Nothing has been decided.

263
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:42,320
As this film is released at the end of September 2026, Michael Smith is due back before Judge Coltl on Tuesday, October 6 at 3pm.

264
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:46,360
It's the same date Rolling Stone once reported for his trial.

265
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,600
Music Business Worldwide describes it as,

266
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:53,380
The first sentence in the US for AI-assisted streaming fraud.

267
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,640
Here is what we'll decide it.

268
00:20:56,320 --> 00:21:00,480
Whether the judge accepts that a drop in an ocean caused no perceptible harm.

269
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:04,420
Where he lands between probation, which the defense wants.

270
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:08,820
The 24 months the probation office recommended, according to billboard.

271
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:13,300
And the 46 to 57 month guideline range billboard reported.

272
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:15,480
All under a five year cap.

273
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:18,100
And whether he orders restitution.

274
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:19,400
And to whom.

275
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,420
Some things are already settled.

276
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:26,140
A federal conviction for conspiracy to commit wire fraud.

277
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:32,700
An eight million dollar money judgment that the government can pursue, including against his other property.

278
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:35,840
Some things may never be known.

279
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:38,180
Who paid most of the money?

280
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:40,960
How much the MLC held back?

281
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:52,580
In 2017, the email in the indictment said 1,040 bots would bring in 1,207,128 dollars a year.

282
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,620
It never had a line for the artists on the other side of the pool.

283
00:21:57,460 --> 00:21:59,820
He did the math on fake streams.

284
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:02,860
The court has already written down one number.

285
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:08,480
8,091,843.64.

286
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:12,320
On October 6th, it writes the rest.

287
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:14,620
That's what it cost.
